JPD wrote:
> Losing one's sight or mobility in nh is common, and indeed being blind
> is sometimes essential.  But sounds also play a big role in the game,
> so becoming deaf would be a big handicap.

Conceptually, this wouldn't be very hard to implement. Adding a
'deafness' attribute, and a couple of causes for it it easy. What would
be an awful lot of work, though, is finding every single sound-related
message in the source and writing an alternative for deaf players.
There are 121 calls to "You_hear()" in pline.c, and that just for
starters.

This idea has been discussed at length a couple of times before. Try
searching google groups for "deafness". I think it's an interesting
idea. I even started trying to implement it at one stage, but it would
be a massive undertaking and requires someone with more time and
patience than I have.

